---
import { REGISTRY_URL } from "@vinui/registry/config"

import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import InstallCommand from "../../../components/InstallCommand.astro"
import PmCommand from "../../../components/PmCommand.astro"
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import { add, create, followedBy, run } from "../../../lib/pm"

const registry = `${REGISTRY_URL}/vue`

const tsconfig = `
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" }
  ],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  }
}`

const tsconfigApp = `
{
  "extends": "@vue/tsconfig/tsconfig.dom.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
    // ...keep the existing options
  }
}`

const viteConfig = `
import { fileURLToPath, URL } from "node:url"
import tailwindcss from "@tailwindcss/vite"
import vue from "@vitejs/plugin-vue"
import { defineConfig } from "vite"

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [vue(), tailwindcss()],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      "@": fileURLToPath(new URL("./src", import.meta.url)),
    },
  },
})`

const app = `
<script setup lang="ts">
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogClose,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogFooter,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogTrigger,
} from "@/components/ui/dialog"
</script>

<template>
  <main class="flex min-h-svh items-center justify-center gap-2">
    <Button>Save</Button>
    <Dialog>
      <DialogTrigger as-child>
        <Button variant="outline">Delete…</Button>
      </DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle>Delete project?</DialogTitle>
          <DialogDescription>This can't be undone.</DialogDescription>
        </DialogHeader>
        <DialogFooter>
          <DialogClose as-child>
            <Button variant="outline">Cancel</Button>
          </DialogClose>
          <DialogClose as-child>
            <Button variant="destructive">Delete</Button>
          </DialogClose>
        </DialogFooter>
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  </main>
</template>`

const registries = `
{
  "registries": {
    "@vinui": "${registry}/{name}.json"
  }
}`
---

<DocsLayout title="Installation · Vue">
  <h1>Installation · Vue</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    vinui is a <a href="https://www.shadcn-vue.com">shadcn-vue</a> style: you use the shadcn-vue CLI and its component API, and get vinui's look. Components are copied into your project, built on <a href="https://reka-ui.com">Reka UI</a> and Tailwind CSS v4.
  </p>
  <p>
    Already using shadcn-vue? Skip to <a href="#existing-project">Existing shadcn-vue project</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="new-project">New project</h2>
  <p>
    This guide uses Vite. For other frameworks, set up Tailwind CSS v4 and the <code>@/</code> import alias as in <a href="https://www.shadcn-vue.com/docs/installation">shadcn-vue's installation guide</a>, then continue from <a href="#init">Initialize vinui</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>1. Create a project</h3>
  <PmCommand commands={followedBy(create("vite", "my-app", "--template vue-ts --no-interactive"), "cd my-app")} />
  <p><code>--no-interactive</code> takes create-vite's defaults instead of asking (it asks about a linter, for example).</p>

  <h3>2. Add Tailwind CSS</h3>
  <PmCommand commands={add("tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite")} />
  <p>Replace everything in <code>src/style.css</code> with:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={`@import "tailwindcss";`} lang="css" file="src/style.css" />

  <h3>3. Set up the <code>@/</code> import alias</h3>
  <p>Add <code>paths</code> to both TypeScript configs:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={tsconfig} lang="json" file="tsconfig.json" />
  <CodeBlock code={tsconfigApp} lang="jsonc" file="tsconfig.app.json" />
  <p>Then add the Tailwind plugin and the alias to Vite:</p>
  <PmCommand commands={add("@types/node", { dev: true })} />
  <CodeBlock code={viteConfig} lang="ts" file="vite.config.ts" />

  <h3 id="init">4. Initialize vinui</h3>
  <InstallCommand framework="vue" args={`init --preset ${registry}/init.json`} />
  <p>
    Pass the URL with <code>--preset</code>; without it, shadcn-vue asks setup questions and ignores vinui's settings. This writes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>components.json</code>, with the <code>@vinui</code> registry already configured</li>
    <li><code>src/lib/utils.ts</code>, the standard <code>cn()</code> helper</li>
    <li>vinui's theme (colors, radius, dark mode) into <code>src/style.css</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    shadcn-vue also adds a few things vinui doesn't use: an Inter font <code>@import</code> at the top of <code>src/style.css</code> (safe to delete), and the <code>@lucide/vue</code> icon package. It installs <code>tw-animate-css</code> too; keep that one, because shadcn-vue imports it whenever you add components.
  </p>

  <h3>5. Add components</h3>
  <InstallCommand framework="vue" args="add @vinui/button @vinui/dialog" />
  <p>
    Each component lands in <code>src/components/ui/</code>, and its styles are added to <code>src/style.css</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>6. Use them</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={app} lang="vue" file="src/App.vue" />
  <PmCommand commands={run("dev")} />

  <h2 id="existing-project">Existing shadcn-vue project</h2>
  <p>vinui components can replace shadcn-vue's one at a time.</p>
  <h3>1. Add the vinui registry</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={registries} lang="json" file="components.json" />
  <h3>2. Add components</h3>
  <InstallCommand framework="vue" args="add @vinui/button" />
  <ul>
    <li>
      If you already have shadcn-vue's version, the CLI asks before overwriting it. vinui uses the same props (<code>variant="outline"</code>, <code>size="sm"</code>, …), so your existing code keeps working.
    </li>
    <li>Your colors are kept; vinui only adds tokens your theme doesn't define yet.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>3. Switch to vinui's colors (optional)</h3>
  <InstallCommand framework="vue" args="add @vinui/theme" />
  <p>
    This <strong>replaces</strong> the values of the tokens vinui defines (<code>--primary</code>, <code>--radius</code>, …) with vinui's. Tokens vinui doesn't define, such as <code>--card</code> or <code>--chart-1</code>, stay as they are.
  </p>

  <h2 id="dark-mode">Dark mode</h2>
  <p>
    Add the <code>dark</code> class to <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>; every component switches to the dark palette.
  </p>

  <h2 id="styling">Styling</h2>
  <p>
    Pass Tailwind classes with <code>class</code>; they override vinui's styles. For state-based styles, use the data attributes Reka UI sets, for example <code>class="data-[state=open]:shadow-xl"</code> on <code>DialogContent</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updating">Updating components</h2>
  <InstallCommand framework="vue" args="add @vinui/button --overwrite" />
  <p>
    The CLI currently appends a component's nested <code>@media</code> and <code>@variant</code> rules again instead of replacing them. Before updating, delete the component's <code>@utility</code> blocks (for example <code>@utility btn</code> …) from <code>src/style.css</code>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
